@startuml resize-frame-sequence
' One step of a window resized by its frame (ledger L9). Colours: orange = the
' compositor, red = the window (winit and blitz-shell), blue = the chrome's own
' code, green = Blitz's layout of the chrome and its pages, yellow = the
' cursor arbiter (crate::cursor), grey = the renderer (crate::renderer, Vello).
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #52687A
  LifeLineBorderColor #52687A
  ParticipantBorderColor #52687A
  GroupBorderColor #52687A
  GroupBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
}
title A window resized by its frame: one size, one frame

participant "Compositor\n(KWin, AppKit, X server)" as comp #FCE4D6
participant "Window\n(winit, blitz-shell)" as window #F8CBAD
participant "ChromeApplication" as app #DDEBF7
participant "ChromeDocument" as chrome #DDEBF7
participant "Blitz resolve\n(chrome, then pages)" as blitz #E2EFDA
participant "PageShell\n+ CursorArbiter" as arbiter #FFF2CC
participant "CoalescingRenderer\n+ Vello" as render #EDEDED

== The pointer takes the window's frame ==
comp -> window : the mouse leaves the surface
window -> app : PointerLeft (mouse)
app -> window : forward (blitz-shell ignores it)
app -> chrome : pointer_left()
chrome -> arbiter : pointer_left(): clear_hover() on the chrome\nand on the page under the pointer (H8)
note right of arbiter
  no position is left to hover:
  later layouts hover nothing
end note

== Each new size ==
comp -> window : new size (Wayland configure,\nAppKit live-resize step, ConfigureNotify)
window -> app : SurfaceResized
app -> window : forward: with_viewport → set_size,\nrequest_redraw, Poll through the proxy
window -> render : set_size(w, h): kept as pending
app -> chrome : View::poll() at once (H7)
chrome -> chrome : render(): the tab strip and the status bar\nare fitted to the new width
app -> chrome : if that changed the chrome: lay_out_now()\n(input before the frame must not meet replaced nodes)
window -> app : RedrawRequested
app -> chrome : begin_paint(): note each page's hovered node
app -> window : forward: View::redraw
window -> blitz : resolve
blitz -> blitz : lay out the chrome
blitz -> arbiter : the page's new viewport asks for a redraw\n(queue_device_changes): set aside (H9)
blitz -> blitz : lay out the page at once, then refresh_hover
window -> render : paint_scene, render
render -> render : apply the pending size (one reconfigure)\nrender, present, wait for the GPU
render -> comp : commit: the buffer of the new size
app -> chrome : end_paint()
chrome -> arbiter : end_paint(): a page asked meanwhile
chrome -> chrome : did a page's hovered node change? no:\nthe frame answered it, so no other frame
window -> app : proxy_wake_up → Poll
app -> chrome : poll(): nothing changed, no frame

group Before L9 (90ad693): two frames for every size
  window -> render : frame A: the chrome still fitted to the old width
  arbiter -> arbiter : repaint: the page's viewport request,\nand its hover at the pointer's last position
  window -> chrome : the proxy's Poll: fit to the new width, repaint
  window -> render : frame B: no layout to do, yet a full render and present
end
@enduml
